Qui sommes-nous ?

Fondée en 2014, Artefact est une société internationale de services autour de l'IA et de la data, spécialisée dans le conseil en IA, transformation data et en data &amp; digital marketing. L’approche unique d’Artefact, qui fait le pont entre la donnée et le business, permet à nos clients d’atteindre leurs objectifs business de façon dédiée et efficace. Nos 2500 collaborateurs répartis dans 27 bureaux à travers le monde allient leurs compétences pluridisciplinaires au profit de l’innovation business des entreprises.&nbsp;

La mission des Artefactors ? Transformer la data de nos clients en impact business. Dans ce sens, nous collaborons avec plus de 1000 clients, leaders de leurs industries (Orange, Carrefour, Samsung, AccorHotels, L’Oréal, LVMH, Decathlon) et sommes partenaires privilégiés de Google (GMP/GCP), AWS ainsi que Microsoft Azure.&nbsp;

En tant que stagiaire Software Engineer, tu seras ammener à:&nbsp;

• Participer activement à la conception et à l'implémentation de solutions techniques robustes et scalables.

• Architecture logicielle : Contribuer à la réflexion sur l'architecture de nos applications, en veillant à la performance et à la maintenabilité du code

• Déploiement et opérations (DevOps) : &nbsp; automatisation des tests et des déploiements cloud avec des pipelines CI/CD et une infrastructure en tant que code (ex : Terraform), packaging d'applications dans des conteneurs (ex : Docker), implémentation d'outils d'observabilité des données (ex : DBT)

• Déploiement de ton logiciel sur le cloud&nbsp; : GCP, AWS ou Azure&nbsp;

• Déploie

Category: IT Services

Location: Fort Western Province Sri Lanka

For an international organization, we are urgently looking for a Full REMOTE Java/Angular Developer. As a Java Developer, you will develop new and expand existing web-based functionalities in a manner that is compatible with the existing IT Platform and ensures Portal compliance.
Candidates need to be willing to work normal office hours in Europe. Example 8 AM European time equals 11:30 AM Sri Lanka time.
During the corona crisis, interviews will be done through WEBEX, and travel is not required for the interviews. All positions are long-term.
Tasks and Responsibilities:

• Perform software quality assurance related activities as part of agile project teams;

• Perform software development related tasks, as required;

• Perform software acceptance testing to ensure that software developed corresponds to functional and non-functional requirements, such as quality-related acceptance criteria and coding standards;

• Perform code reviews and code related testing activities as per confirmed quality assurance requirements;

Profile:

• Bachelor or Master degree;

• +5 years working as experience in Java;

• Experience in programming using Angular;

• Experience in programming using Javascript; HTML; CSS and other platforms;

• Knowledge of Amazon AWS development environments is an advantage;

• Experience in performing software quality assurance activities (i.e. unit, integration, and end-to-end testing, peer reviews, etc.);

• Knowledge and experience of iterative/agile project delivery methods;

Interested :

If you have the right profile, you have the opportunity to be a part of a dynamic team working for a company with global exposure, providing you a great working environment and ample space to learn and develop. If you are ready to grab this opportunity, please forward your CV to or call us on +94 114312515 for more information.

